This image, combining Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) and Dynamic Light Scattering (DLS) data, characterizes the Nano-11 nanoparticles. The TEM micrograph on the left reveals spherical particles with an irregular, cauliflower-like surface, while the DLS graph on the right demonstrates a narrow size distribution, indicating a consistent average hydrodynamic diameter of 75-80 nm for Nano-11, which supports its role as an effective vaccine adjuvant due to its uniform nanoparticle size.